# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# scan output — JSONL logs may contain evidence bytes from live targets; treat like a fuzzer's
# crash corpus, never publish or commit
output/
*.jsonl
*.csv
*-report.html
# exception: this is a maintained lab-notes tracking file (which ingest/ files have been
# reviewed, safe to remove), not generated scan output — added 2026-09-15
!lab-notes/ingest-review-status.csv

# never store real secrets locally regardless of the keyring policy (target.py rejects
# plaintext creds in the inventory itself, but keep any local cryptfile-backend file out too)
*.cryptfile
cryptfile_pass.cfg

# working copies of externally-supplied credential material a check needs at runtime but must
# NEVER commit — e.g. checks/ssh/native/ssh_hardcoded_private_key.py's private_key_path param.
# Added 2026-09-14 for the Bosch Rexroth Nexo CVE-2023-48251 check: the key itself is a real,
# working universal-root credential for a currently-deployed product, independently extracted
# from public firmware — this directory is where an operator's own local copy lives, referenced
# by path from a check's params, never embedded in the params/YAML itself or git history.
# secrets/README.md is the one exception — it's documentation (the naming convention + the
# move-between-machines playbook), not secret material, and needs to actually ship with the repo
# for anyone who clones it to see it. Caught 2026-09-14: the original blanket `secrets/` pattern
# below would have silently excluded that README from git too — fixed before it was ever committed.
secrets/*
!secrets/README.md

# third-party vendor manuals dropped in for research (e.g. GE Multilin PDFs) — a real, sizable
# working directory, but copyrighted vendor documents, not project content; never commit
ingest/

# editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
unblob.log

# password-cracking session artifacts (John the Ripper / hashcat): pot files, recovery/restore
# state, and session logs. These can contain target hashes and recovered plaintexts; they are
# transient run artifacts, never project content. Prefer running crackers from the scratchpad,
# but ignore them here as a backstop. (Caught 2026-10-28: a stray John session log,
# deltacrk2.log, landed at the repo root during a Delta hash-verification run.)
*.pot
*.rec
*.restore
/*.log
lab-notes/*.csv.bak-*

# Office owner-lock temp files (created when a doc is open)
~$*

# bundled exploitability feed (public FIRST EPSS, refreshed via scripts/build_exploit_intel.sh)
!core/data/epss.csv
dist/
